# onTrack session (always-on)

Keep this file short on purpose. Load detail only when the task needs it.

## When to load more

| Task | Read |
|------|------|
| App UI / simulator / screenshot bug | `.cursor/skills/agent-ui/SKILL.md` **before** verify |
| Hang / slow / stuck sim, emu, verify, pool, Metro device | **`docs/agent-ui-verify-benchmark.md` first** (H1–H19 + TSV), then agent-ui skill + `stuck-check-config.mdc` |
| Design / polish / “make it cool” | `~/.cursor/skills/think-cool/SKILL.md` |
| Cleanup / “optimize” | `~/.cursor/skills/optimize-code/SKILL.md` |
| Domain feature work | `.cursor/skills/<domain>/` (travel, todos, workouts, …) + `AGENTS.md` feature table |
| Form field icons / numeric inputs / migrations | matching `.cursor/rules/*` via globs |

## Non-negotiables (every session)

- **No personal identifiers** in source — see `no-personal-identifiers.mdc`.
- **Bug fixes require direct + surrounding regression tests** in the same change — see `bug-fix-regression-tests.mdc`; cover the reported failure plus adjacent/boundary/recurrence cases, and backfill missing coverage when touching an older fix.
- **Device testing is opt-in only** → never boot, open, or use a simulator, emulator, physical device, `agent-ui`, or dual-platform UI verification unless the user explicitly requests device testing in the current task. App-affecting JS/UI defaults to typecheck + focused tests. If device testing is requested, use `./scripts/agent-ui-verify-both.sh --route … [--flow <name>] --exists …`, assert/`--color`, then stop.
- **Headless verify** → dedicated agent devices only (`onTrack Agent N` / `onTrack_Agent_N`, **max 2 per platform**). No slot free → exit 3, report the skip, stop without testing. Never touch `onTrack iPhone 17 Pro` / `Galaxy_S26`; no headed handoff. Headed Simulator/AVD only if the user asks. Launch >30s = defect to fix. After testing: **safe shutdown** on lease EXIT (`KEEP_IOS`/`KEEP_ANDROID=0` default; Android `default_boot` snapshot first). Never leave agent devices orphaned (reap on claim). Park-warm only with `KEEP_*=1`.
- **Agent accounts** → `./scripts/agent-ui.sh login` dismisses prompts then signs into the slot’s `agent_N` account (dev-only, `account_flags.agent_test`); `--guest` for credential-free runs. Credentials only in `.env.local` (`./scripts/agent-accounts-setup.sh` or `ONTRACK_AGENT_LOGIN_EMAIL`/`PASSWORD` override — never commit personal emails).
- **Dev Mode** → off by default (cold start clears hub + agent sandboxes). Seeds/flows may turn it on for mock data; `verify-both` / `agent-ui.sh devmode release` turn agent sandboxes off again. Do not leave it on.
- **Glyph / icon orientation** → fix from source (`Symbol`, `design-system/icons.ts`, platform maps, transforms). Never screenshot→vision loops for micro-glyphs; do not force-reconnect to “re-check” icons.
- **New/edited interactive controls** → `ontrack.*` `testID` + `ids.ts` + `docs/agent-ui-map.md` in the same change.
- **New/edited user journeys** → add/update the named recipe in `src/utils/agent-ui/flows-*.ts`; the Living System Map watches these sources and adds the ordered journey plus its testing gaps automatically.
- **Dump = debt** → ≤1 dump to discover; same turn stamp id/map and/or named flow so that dump is never needed again (agent-ui skill).
- **Metro** → `npm run packager:ensure:start` (never `npm start` in agent shells). Prefer Fast Refresh; do not kill Metro / `--clear` / force-stop / `--force-reconnect` after routine edits. Node 24.
- **Stuck / slow / device timeout** → stop grinding. Benchmark first → classify once via stuck-check / agent-ui skill; fix the cause so it does not recur.
- **Locality** → smallest entry file first; extract if touched file would stay >700 lines; prefer Shared patterns in `AGENTS.md`.
- **Responsive chrome** → `useResponsive()` + `AppText fit` (see `responsive-layout.mdc`).
- **Glass UI** → see `glass-ui.mdc` (product chrome is glass; no opaque paper fills).
- **Think cool** → UI should feel crafted/delightful (presence, one idea, restraint); for design/polish read `~/.cursor/skills/think-cool/SKILL.md`.
- **Smooth transitions** → continuous / eased motion over abrupt snaps; never break functionality or fluidity (Development `.cursor/rules/smooth-transitions.mdc`).
- **Optimize** → cleanup/rename/reuse/token-slim/temp removal; read `~/.cursor/skills/optimize-code/SKILL.md`.
- **`push`** → always `npm run ship:push -- -m "<concise why>"` (`scripts/ship-push.sh`). Same for “push script” / “ship push”. Flow: patch-bump `.xx` + release notes/changelog → commit → branch → PR → merge main → delete branch → TestFlight + device OTA (no APK). Do **not** treat bare `push` as plain git push. Use `--ota-only` to reship current main (no bump); `--skip-ota` to skip EAS Update. Native / `runtimeVersion` binary → `android:release-to-drive` / `build:device:android` separately.
